# apps/landing — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and edit. Every variable the landing app reads is
# listed here; all are OPTIONAL and the app builds and runs with none of them set.
# Vite only exposes `VITE_`-prefixed variables to client code.

# Let the browser re-fetch the social-proof stats (GitHub stars, npm weekly
# downloads) on mount, refreshing the values baked in at build time by
# `yarn build:stats`.
#
# OFF by default, and deliberately so: until the GitHub repo and the npm package
# are public, both endpoints 404 — and the browser logs those failures itself, so
# no try/catch in our code can keep the console clean. The build-time values in
# `src/generated/liveStats.ts` render either way; this only controls the client
# refresh on top of them. Flip it to `true` once the package is published.
#
# Read by: src/composables/useLiveStats.ts
# VITE_ENABLE_LIVE_STATS=true

# Turn on every surface whose flow ends in `npm install @dzup-ui/*`:
#   • "Open in StackBlitz" on the block and template detail pages — the forked
#     project installs `@dzup-ui/core|tokens|contracts` from npm.
#   • The copy-paste MCP configs on /ai — they run `npx -y @dzup-ui/mcp`.
#
# OFF by default for the same reason the stats refresh is: the packages are not
# published yet, so both flows end in a 404 the visitor sees. While it's off,
# each surface renders an inline note saying the action lands at the v0.1
# publish; the source stays copyable throughout. Flip this and
# VITE_ENABLE_LIVE_STATS together the day the packages go live.
#
# Read by: src/lib/publishState.ts
# VITE_PACKAGES_PUBLISHED=true
